y busy  i've also been doing a bit more writing  in medium and of course being on the the  radio shows that i co-host wisdom for  life and drive time from river west  uh did some interviews as well  um we had  massimo pigliucci on the drive time show  we had  donald robertson on wisdom for life  and i've also had a lot of tutorial  clients a lot of new clients and a lot  of old clients some consulting some  philosophical counseling so that has  been  you know making my days pretty pretty  packed i did get to the gym  uh quite a few times although as i got  sick and very very tired  that  has hasn't been the case for the last  week or so right  videos i shot a number of videos i got  three half hour hegel videos in the  religion section done one book review  video i did another one of those wombo  taking you know a prompt using my  master's thesis  uh hussarl's  passive synthesis and the constitution  of language as a prompt so i did i did  that as well  there's videos from all the events which  you can easily find by clicking the show  more or video description i'll put links  to all of those  below  i did some sadler's stories videos and i  also released a number of the  earthsea  videos those were from tales from  earthsea  and  i finished up with core concept videos  on foucault on the subject in power and  that's what led me into deciding to  focus on that for the political theory  and application discussion  i i also did a contest  having to do with a podcast  saying what should we do  should we  do aristotle should we do deluge should  we do anselm should we do aj air and you  know i'm actually going to do all of  them it was just a question of what  order and i was very surprised to see  that aristotle's politics book one  took precedence and  people really got into that  so  that's what i started doing  last month after i finished up with all  the other podcast stuff that i was  releasing and working on so busy busy  month um you know again  uh cut short in 